      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Co removal reduces stacking-fault energy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At high strain rates and/or low temperatures, FeNiCrMn switches from primarily dislocation slip to twinning-assisted deformation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increased lattice distortion promotes deformation twinning over simple dislocation slip.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower stacking-fault energy promotes deformation twinning at high strain rates and low temperatures.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deformation twins provide a secondary mode for accommodating plastic strain.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Twinning maintains strength while enhancing dynamic ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed twinning-assisted mechanism preserves a favorable strength–ductility balance.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial FeNiCrMn material is fully homogenized and is a single-phase solid solution.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At high strain rates and low temperatures, FeNiCrMn will develop a higher deformation-twin density than equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi tested under identical conditions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under those conditions, FeNiCrMn will retain more ductility than the Co-containing baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under those conditions, FeNiCrMn will have strength comparable to the Co-containing baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The enhanced-twinning regime is expected to extend from cryogenic temperature to room temperature when stacking-fault energy is sufficiently low.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The enhanced-twinning mechanism is expected under dynamic loading.",
